Top-down dungeon map, dark fantasy style, ink and parchment aesthetic. Underground abandoned level, dim green bioluminescent light from fungi on walls. Water puddles on stone floor. Seven distinct areas connected by corridors. Central hub: irregular room with three exits (east, west, south). East wing: short corridor ending at a wooden door (suspiciously clean and well-maintained, polished handle), behind it a room divided by iron grate (cell on one side with straw, storage on other side with rotting crates and chains). West wing: small antechamber with well shaft opening in floor, then large 30ft square room with scattered objects (a pristine wooden chair perfectly centered, a clean ladder against west wall, an overturned table, a hanging chain, a wall candelabra, a closed chest in corner). South corridor: small room with graffiti-covered walls, then narrow passage with slightly different colored floor tile (trap), ending at descending stairs. A breach in the north wall of the main corridor reveals a tunnel leading away (sewer connection). Green-tinted dim lighting throughout, stalactites dripping. Grid overlay 5ft squares. No text, no labels.
